/T (ESG Performance Impact. Our analysis shows that TSEL, with an ESG score of 8.6 \(Figure 32\), is a strong performer, warranting a 100 bps ESG discount to its cost of equity due to its lower ESG risk profile. In contrast, MTEL records an ESG score of 8.1 \(Figure 33\), classifying it as a moderate performer with ESG risks aligned to the industry average; therefore, no adjustment to its cost of equity is applied.)
